"""Most of the table's codes for these instances are not at a local optimum of the largest cosine. Local search from the
published coordinates lowered the cosine of 40 of the 49 by more than 1e-12 and of 28 by more than 1e-6, by up to
2.6e-04 (9_223); 40 of them beat the table's displayed (rounded-up) cosine by at least 1e-12. The search per instance:
sequential linear programming on the near-active pairs (sph.maximize), L-BFGS on the smooth maximum of the cosines
at sharpness rising to 1e9 (sph.descend), and basin hopping (sph.improve: shake all points by 1e-4 to 1e-2 of the
minimal chord, descend, maximize, keep drops), in passes of a few minutes each, about half an hour per instance in
all. It does not converge: a further minute of descend and maximize still lowers the cosine by up to about 4e-7 on
24 of the 49. Instances where nothing beat the published code keep it. These codes are the bar the task
scores against. COS2 is the exact signed squared cosine of the binary64 points as numerator/denominator, COORDS the
points as base64 of little-endian binary64 rows."""

